# Full-stack feature development

This app uses an Angular frontend and a Flask backend (separate repo). When adding or changing API-backed behaviour:

1. **One feature, both sides**: Implement or update the backend endpoint and the Angular service/model in the same flow so request/response shapes stay aligned.
2. **Contract first**: Define method, path, and request/response shape; then implement backend route and frontend types in `src/app/models/` and the call in `src/app/services/`.
3. **Naming and types**: Use the same field names and types (string, number, boolean, arrays) in Flask JSON and TypeScript interfaces.
4. **Document backend source**: In `src/app/models/*.ts`, add a short comment referencing the backend route (e.g. "See tasks() in flask/app.py in hevelius-backend").
5. **API base**: All URLs use `Hevelius.apiUrl` from `src/hevelius.ts` (e.g. `Hevelius.apiUrl + '/your-path'`).

See project root **AGENTS.md** for the full API overview and workflow.
